# Environment files. Phase 12 Secret Handling audit: the previous rules
# (.env, .env.local, .env.*.local, .env.production.local) never covered
# Firebase's own documented convention for per-project Functions secrets
# deployed via `firebase deploy` — files named functions/.env.<project-id>
# (e.g. functions/.env.brainwise-ai-marketing-engine) or a bare
# functions/.env.staging/.env.production with no ".local" suffix. None of
# those names matched any existing rule, so if one were ever created for a
# real deploy, `git add -A` would happily stage real plaintext secrets. A
# broad `.env.*` closes that for every current and future dotenv naming
# variant; `.env.example` is explicitly un-ignored since it's the tracked,
# secret-free template every other .env file is copied from.
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example

